CONTENT
Playbook ID: RD-005. Title: "RD-005: Non-Frontend Requests Stay Off the Frontend Surface".
What it verifies: requests that share a word with frontend work, such as padding, hover, easing, transition, contrast or shadow, but concern other code, never return sk-code-frontend. The risk it guards: bare single-word keywords once matched inside unrelated sentences and sent binary, shell and language-server work to the frontend references.
Realistic user request: a developer asks for backend or tooling work whose wording happens to contain a frontend-sounding word.
Exact prompt (the first of the set, used for the "Exact prompt" block and the "Prompt:" line):
add left padding to the binary buffer before hashing
The full prompt set, which section 3 replays, one per line:
add left padding to the binary buffer before hashing
hover over the symbol to debug the typescript type error
pad the string with zeros in the python formatter
easing the migration of the shell scripts to bash 5
the transition between workflow states fails in the reducer
add a hover provider to the language server
fix the contrast stretch in the image processing python script
the shadow copy of the config file is stale
Preconditions: node is callable, and `node .skilled/bin/compiled-route-guard.cjs --json` reports the sk-code hub as fresh.
Exact Command Sequence: 1. save the 8 prompts, one per line, to /tmp/skc-RD005-prompts.txt. 2. run: while IFS= read -r p; do node .skilled/bin/compiled-route.cjs --hub sk-code --prompt "$p"; done < /tmp/skc-RD005-prompts.txt > /tmp/skc-RD005-routes.txt  3. run: grep -c '"workflowMode":"sk-code-frontend"' /tmp/skc-RD005-routes.txt
Expected signals: 8 decision lines. A line may be a defer or a route to another packet such as sk-code-skilled. The count command prints 0 and exits 1.
PASS iff the count is 0. FAIL iff any decision names sk-code-frontend.
Evidence: /tmp/skc-RD005-routes.txt
Failure triage: 1. Find the failing prompt's line in the routes file. 2. List the frontend keywords with no space and no hyphen: node -e "const v=require('./.skilled/skills/sk-code/hub-router.json').vocabularyClasses;console.log(Object.keys(v).filter(c=>c.startsWith('code-frontend')).flatMap(c=>v[c].keywords).filter(k=>!/[ -]/.test(k)))" 3. Replace each single-word keyword it prints with a phrase of two or more words, in hub-router.json and in the INTENT_SIGNALS rows of both ROUTER.md files. 4. If the list is empty, a phrase is too broad, so narrow the phrase that matched. Never edit a prompt to make it pass.

VERIFY (run from the repository root):
grep -c '^## [1-5]\. ' .skilled/skills/sk-code/manual-testing-playbook/routing-disambiguation/frontend-negative-probes.md
